      ],
      "source": "https://fillmorecity.org/about-us/",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "From 1851 to 1856, Fillmore served as Utah Territory's capital, though the legislature convened there only once in 1855.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5,
        18,
        29
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fillmore%2C_Utah",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The original Utah Territorial Statehouse still stands in Fillmore, a relic of early statehood.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        19
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fillmore%2C_Utah",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Fillmore sits in the Pahvant Valley, just below the foothills of the Pahvant Mountain Range.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        30
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fillmore%2C_Utah",
      "category": "nature",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Heritage, families and legends converge along the historic Pony Express route that winds through Utah's West Desert.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        14
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.visitutah.com/places-to-go/cities-and-towns/fillmore",
      "category": "culture",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
